From d0ab656ed1376995c9bc8562866166f4b64bf701 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:15:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Isolate proof backend homes before bootstrap
 consumers

gateway-9aaf151a15: a restart-proof backend (serve --isolated + HERMES_DESKTOP=1)
started by an agent on the real home ran startup recovery and adopted an
unrelated chat; the probe's SIGTERM then interrupted it. Endpoint isolation
was never state isolation.

- hermes_cli/proof_home.py (stdlib + hermes_constants/_parser only):
  `hermes serve|dashboard --proof-home DIR` or HERMES_PROOF_HOME selects
  HERMES_HOME in hermes_bootstrap, after tree repair and before scratch export,
  config or recovery. DIR must be an existing disposable directory, never the
  production root, root/profiles/* or the launching agent home
  (HERMES_AGENT_HOME), resolved through aliases/symlinks; not combinable with
  --profile. Invalid -> exit 2 with a safe recipe, before any write.
- Agent-originated restart-proof shapes (--isolated or HERMES_DESKTOP=1 with
  HERMES_AGENT_TOOL_CALL / HERMES_AGENT_ORIGIN / HERMES_KANBAN_TASK /
  HERMES_KANBAN_WORKER_TASK / HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_CONTEXT) on a production
  home exit 2. Absent stamps change nothing: Desktop (incl. SSH token-file)
  and always-on backends keep today's behaviour; --status/--stop/--help pass.
- web_server re-checks before the server/lifespan consumers start.
- Tool children (terminal, process, execute_code) are stamped with
  HERMES_AGENT_TOOL_CALL=1, HERMES_AGENT_ORIGIN and HERMES_AGENT_HOME after env
  scrubbing; the SSH terminal backend re-exports the origin remotely.
- Defense in depth: startup_resume and process re-adoption refuse production
  state from an agent/proof backend; a proof home still recovers its OWN jobs.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_serve_proof_home.py (+ _recovery: real serve,
SIGTERM/restart, own job re-adopted, sentinel untouched).
